            <ArticleTitle>[Acute coronary syndrome in a female patient with multilevel atherosclerosis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1287-90; discussion 1291</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of 74-years-old woman who was admitted to Department of Interventional Cardiology due to acute coronary syndrome is presented. The multilevel atherosclerosis was diagnosed. The patient was successfully treated with two-stage percutaneous coronary and peripheral revascularisation. During 6-months follow-up patient was in good condition.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
